    "question": "Let |A| = 3 and |B| = 4. How many onto (surjective) functions f : A → B exist?",
    "options": {
      "A": "0",
      "B": "12",
      "C": "24",
      "D": "64"
    },
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "explanation": "A function can be onto only if every element of B is hit by at least one element of A. Since |A| < |B|, this is impossible, so the count is 0.",
