    "question": "A relation R on the set {1,2,3,4} is known to be reflexive and antisymmetric. Which of the following statements must be true?",
    "options": {
      "A": "R is also symmetric.",
      "B": "R contains the ordered pair (2,3).",
      "C": "R contains (a,a) for every a in the set.",
      "D": "R is transitive."
    },
    "correct_answer": "C",
    "explanation": "Reflexivity guarantees that (a,a) belongs to R for every element a of the set. Antisymmetry does not force symmetry or transitivity, and no specific off‑diagonal pair is required.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
